2026-09-13. Independent source review of pipe 2fb5c33f and connection b39a29ce found three failure paths before any qualification. The exact pipe and case drafts are retained under drafts.

A frame can complete one chunk and then fail in the next deadline or allocation. Whole-frame errors now quarantine the pair so later frames cannot continue a desynchronized stream. An operation record is published before event or OVERLAPPED creation; setup failure closes a recorded event where confirmed, retaining any uncertain owner. This does not claim an atomic bridge across arbitrary interruption between a scalar-returning Win32 API and Python recording its return; that remains a narrow FFI/platform observation concern for the dummy test protocol.

Quarantine now attempts one bounded stop through the retained worker's existing partial-cleanup path. It records only whether that exact process wait returned success. It never marks the worker quiescent, clears uncertainty, releases file guards, or frees an unconfirmed OVERLAPPED buffer. A process wait alone does not prove the owned job is empty or pending parent I/O has completed. Failure cleanup remains conservative even if the stop attempt succeeds.

The child read-handle mapping is still held only in the controller record. Reconstruction of an owned child ReadSet/BufferAssets from a fixed, authenticated manifest map and queried handle identities is not implemented. The first dummy worker will only exchange generated messages and keep inherited file handles alive; it will not read model bytes or claim that missing handoff is complete. This limitation is separate from the still-unreviewed CTranslate2 reader.
